{{Documentation/Header}}
Lists every utaite whose birthday falls on a given month and day, as a grid of {{T|BirthdayEntry}} cards. This is the "Birthdays!" block on [[Utaite Wiki]] and [[Youtaite Wiki]].

== How the birthday system works ==
Birthdays are not stored in a list — they are derived from infoboxes:

# {{T|Utaite}} adds <code><nowiki>[[Category:Birthday/MM/DD]]</nowiki></code> to a page when <code>birthmonth</code>, <code>birthday</code> '''and <code>birthref</code>''' are all filled in. Without a birth reference the page is instead filed under [[:Category:Utaite with Missing Birth Reference]] and '''will not appear in any birthday listing'''.
# This template runs a DPL query for that category.
# Each matching page is passed to {{T|ProcessSingerPage/Birthday}}, which reads <code>image</code>, <code>birthyear</code>, <code>birthmonth</code> and <code>birthday</code> back off that page's infobox using <code><nowiki>{{#invoke:Utaite|getParameter}}</nowiki></code>.
# Those values are rendered by {{T|BirthdayEntry}}.

Pages in [[:Category:Deceased Utaite]] are always excluded.

See {{T|Birthday Calendar}} for the whole-month view, which uses a separate query path.

== Syntax ==
{{T|ProcessBirthdayCategory|block=1
|v1=month =
|v2=day =
|v3=cat =
|v4=includeMMDD =
}}

== Examples ==
Today's birthdays, as used on the main page:
<pre>{{ProcessBirthdayCategory|includeMMDD=false|month={{CURRENTJSTMONTH}}|day={{CURRENTJSTDAY}}}}</pre>

A fixed date, with the MM/DD heading shown:
<pre>{{ProcessBirthdayCategory|includeMMDD=true|month=06|day=30}}</pre>

Restricted to youtaite, as used on [[Youtaite Wiki]]:
<pre>{{ProcessBirthdayCategory|cat=Youtaite|includeMMDD=false|month={{CURRENTJSTMONTH}}|day={{CURRENTJSTDAY}}}}</pre>

{| class="dataTable sortable"
! Parameter !! Aliases !! Label !! Description !! Type !! Default !! Status
|-
| <code>month</code> || – || Month || Month to match, '''zero-padded to two digits'''. See the note below. || number || – || <span style="color:red;font-weight:bold;">Required</span>
|-
| <code>day</code> || – || Day || Day to match, '''zero-padded to two digits'''. || number || – || <span style="color:red;font-weight:bold;">Required</span>
|-
| <code>cat</code> || – || Category filter || Restricts results to pages in a category ending with this text. Matched as an SQL suffix, so <code>Utaite</code> also matches "Male Utaite" and "Female Utaite". || string || Utaite ||
|-
| <code>includeMMDD</code> || – || Show date heading || Set to <code>true</code> to add an <code>MM/DD</code> heading above the timestamp. || string || – ||
|}

=== Zero-padding matters ===
{{T|Utaite}} builds the category with <code>padleft</code>, so it is always <code>Birthday/06/30</code> — never <code>Birthday/6/30</code>. Passing <code>month=6</code> silently matches nothing. Always use <code>06</code>.

Because <code><nowiki>{{CURRENTJSTMONTH}}</nowiki></code> and <code><nowiki>{{CURRENTJSTDAY}}</nowiki></code> are already zero-padded, the main-page calls are safe as written.

== Output ==
A timestamp line in JST (<code>YYYY年MM月DD日（曜）HH:MM</code>) built from {{T|CURRENTJSTYEAR}}, {{T|CURRENTJSTMONTH}}, {{T|CURRENTJSTDAY}}, {{T|CURRENTJSTDOWJAP}}, {{T|CURRENTJSTHOUR}} and {{T|CURRENTMINUTE}}, followed by a grid of birthday cards. When nobody matches, it shows ''"No stars☆彡 were born on this day"''.

